skill: "google-flow"
sections[19]:
  - "\n"
  - "# Google Flow (Headless Video Generation & Automation)\n\nAutomate video generation, tile inspection, Scene Builder extensions, and media downloading from **Google Flow** via `google-flow-mcp`. All operations execute strictly headless through Obscura CDP without launching visible Chrome windows.\n\n"
  - "## Core Operating Invariants\n\n1. **Headless Execution Only (Zero Visible Browser Windows)**:\n   - Chrome/Obscura must run strictly headless (`FLOW_MCP_HEADLESS=true`, `FLOW_MCP_USE_OBSCURA=1`) via [google-flow-mcp.sh](../../../mcp/google-flow-mcp.sh).\n   - Use dedicated user data directory `~/.obscura-flow-profile` or `~/.google-flow-chrome`.\n   - Never launch standard desktop Chrome windows or interfere with the user's active browsing session.\n\n2. **Skill-First Research & Prompt Crafting Protocol**:\n   - Never generate raw or speculative prompts directly from user queries.\n   - Consult specialist skills and generate structured prompts via `bin/agyos video veo-prompt` before calling Flow:\n     - [veo-3](../veo-3/SKILL.md): Director prompt anatomy and audio cues.\n     - [ai-video](../ai-video/SKILL.md): The BRIEF framework (portable specifications, duration pacing).\n     - [scripting-and-storyboarding](../scripting-and-storyboarding/SKILL.md): Scene breakdowns and shot lists.\n     - [video-production-orchestrator](../video-production-orchestrator/SKILL.md): End-to-end assembly, repair, and film finishing.\n\n3. **Dry-Run Gate & Mandatory Local Verification**:\n   - Always call `flow_generate_video` / `flow_generate_image` / `flow_scene_extend` with `auto_confirm: false` first to inspect the prepared prompt and screenshot before spending credits.\n   - Save outputs locally (`flow_<media_id>_<job_id>.mp4`) and verify with `bin/agyos video self-eval <video.mp4> --json`.\n\n---\n\n"
  - "## Google Flow MCP Architecture\n\n- **Upstream MCP Server**: [ParkSangGwon/google-flow-mcp](https://github.com/ParkSangGwon/google-flow-mcp) (`@park-sang-gwon/google-flow-mcp`)\n- **Launcher Script**: [mcp/google-flow-mcp.sh](../../../mcp/google-flow-mcp.sh)\n- **Watermark Helper**: [scripts/remove_flow_watermark.py](../../../scripts/remove_flow_watermark.py)\n- **CDP Debug Port**: `9333` (via `bin/obscura cdp --port 9333`)\n\n"
  - "### Environment Variables\n```bash\nFLOW_MCP_CHROME_PATH=\"./bin/obscura\"\nFLOW_MCP_USER_DATA_DIR=\"$HOME/.obscura-flow-profile\"\nFLOW_MCP_PROFILE_DIRECTORY=\"Default\"\nFLOW_MCP_CDP_PORT=\"9333\"\nFLOW_MCP_STATE_DIR=\"$HOME/.google-flow-mcp\"\nFLOW_MCP_HEADLESS=\"true\"\nFLOW_MCP_USE_OBSCURA=\"1\"\n```\n\n---\n\n"
  - "## MCP Tools Reference\n\n"
  - "### 1. `flow_generate_video`\nGenerates a video through the Google Flow agent composer and downloads the completed MP4.\n\nParameters:\n- `prompt` (string, required): Full directed scene description including cinematography, action, lighting, and explicit audio cues.\n- `model` (string, default: `veo-3.1-fast`): Veo model variant (`veo-3.1-quality`, `veo-3.1-fast`, `veo-3.1-lite`, `omni-flash`).\n- `ratio` (string, default: `9:16`): Aspect ratio (`9:16` vertical, `16:9` widescreen).\n- `duration` (integer, default: `8`): Clip duration in seconds (`4`, `6`, `8`, `10` where `10` is Omni Flash only).\n- `project_url` (string, required): Destination project URL (`https://flow.google.com/project/<project_id>`).\n- `output_dir` (string, required): Local path where the MP4 will be downloaded (`flow_<id8>_<job>.mp4`).\n- `auto_confirm` (boolean, default: `false`): Set `false` to dry-run/preview; set `true` to commit credits and generate.\n- `reference_images` (array of strings, optional): Local file paths for first-frame, first+last frame, or Ingredients-to-Video conditioning (up to 3 references).\n- `edit_mode` (boolean, default: `false`): Edit the last video of the active session instead of generating a new one.\n- `resume` (boolean, optional): Set `true` to reconnect to an in-flight job.\n- `job_id` (string, optional): Specific job ID to resume after restart.\n\n"
  - "### 2. `flow_scene_add` (Scene Builder Initialization)\nCreates a new multi-clip Scene Builder timeline from an existing project media asset.\n\nParameters:\n- `project_url` (string, required): Destination project URL.\n- `media_id` (string, required): The 8-character media ID or title of the base video clip.\nReturns: `scene_url`, `scene_id`, and initial clip timeline.\n\n"
  - "### 3. `flow_scene_extend` (Scene Builder Extension)\nGenerates a 7-second continuation (Veo 3.1 Lite) of the last clip in the scene timeline with frame-exact seam continuity (NCC ~0.995-0.998) and synchronized audio. Restate subject, wardrobe, lighting, and camera move in every hop prompt because Flow does not carry previous prompts forward.\n\nParameters:\n- `scene_url` (string, required): Scene URL returned by `flow_scene_add`.\n- `prompt` (string, required): Narrative description of what happens next in the scene.\n- `after_clip_index` (integer, required): Index of the clip to extend (0-based; must be the last clip).\n- `output_dir` (string, required): Local target folder for downloading the extension clip.\n- `auto_confirm` (boolean, default: `false`): `false` dry-runs and takes screenshot; `true` commits credits and generates.\n- `resume` (boolean, optional): Set `true` to reconnect to an in-flight extension.\n\n"
  - "### 4. `flow_scene_status`\nReads the current timeline clips, total duration, and rendering status of an active Scene Builder scene.\n\nParameters:\n- `scene_url` (string, required): Scene URL.\n\n"
  - "### 5. `flow_generate_image`\nGenerates high-resolution images via Nano Banana models for video reference conditioning, first/last keyframes, or thumbnails.\n\nParameters:\n- `prompt` (string, required): Visual description.\n- `model` (string, default: `nano-banana-pro`): Image model variant (`nano-banana-pro`, `nano-banana-2`, `nano-banana-2-lite`).\n- `ratio` (string, default: `16:9`): Aspect ratio (`16:9`, `9:16`, `1:1`, `4:3`, `3:4`).\n- `project_url` (string, required): Flow project URL.\n- `output_dir` (string, required): Local directory for downloaded image.\n- `auto_confirm` (boolean, default: `false`): Commit generation.\n\n"
  - "### 6. `flow_project_open` & `flow_inspect`\nOpens and inspects the Google Flow project canvas headlessly, returning project title, media count, tiles, and UI element snapshots.\n\n"
  - "### 7. `flow_media_download`\nDownloads a specific media asset from the Flow project by UUID.\n\nParameters:\n- `media_id` (string, required): Asset identifier.\n- `output_dir` (string, required): Target folder on disk.\n- `suffix` (string, default: `manual`): Filename suffix.\n\n"
  - "### 8. `flow_status` & `flow_connect`\nChecks the current CDP connection state, login status, active session, and running jobs.\n\n---\n\n"
  - "## Veo 3.1 Official Prompting & Creative Workflows\n\n1. **5-Part Director Formula**: `[Cinematography] + [Subject] + [Action] + [Context] + [Style & Ambiance]` plus `[Soundstage]` (quoted dialogue, SFX, ambient noise).\n2. **First & Last Frame Transitions**: Generate start and end stills with `flow_generate_image`, pass both in `reference_images`, and describe the camera arc connecting them.\n3. **Ingredients to Video**: Pass up to 3 reference images (character, prop, setting) to lock identity across multi-shot dialogue or product scenes.\n4. **Timestamp Prompting**: Direct multi-beat pacing inside one 8s clip using `[00:00-00:02] ... [00:02-00:04] ... [00:04-00:08] ...`.\n5. **Positive Negative-Prompting**: Describe absence positively (e.g. `\"empty desert road with clear horizon\"` instead of `\"no buildings or cars\"`).\n\nGenerate structured prompts directly with:\n```bash\nbin/agyos video veo-prompt \"<scene idea>\" --ratio 9:16 --duration 8 --style cinema --json\n```\n\n---\n\n"
  - "## Workflow: From Query to Organic Cinema Master\n\n```text\n1. Prompt Engineering  -> bin/agyos video veo-prompt \"<idea>\" --ratio 9:16 --json\n2. Dry-Run Gate        -> flow_generate_video (auto_confirm: false) -> inspect screenshot\n3. Headless Generation -> flow_generate_video (auto_confirm: true) -> flow_<id8>_<job>.mp4\n4. Scene Extension     -> flow_scene_add -> flow_scene_extend (7s hops) -> ffmpeg concat\n5. Watermark Removal   -> uv run scripts/remove_flow_watermark.py raw.mp4 delogo.mp4\n6. Defect Repair       -> uv run scripts/repair_ai_video.py full delogo.mp4 -o repaired.mp4\n7. Organic Film Finish -> uv run scripts/organic_film_engine.py master repaired.mp4 -o final.mp4\n8. Self-Eval Gate      -> bin/agyos video self-eval final.mp4 --json\n```\n\n---\n\n"
  - "## Automated Watermark Removal Workflow\n\nVeo video generations include a small corner indicator mark in the bottom-right corner. Apply localized delogo inpainting via:\n\n```bash\nuv run scripts/remove_flow_watermark.py <input_video.mp4> [output_clean.mp4]\n```\n\n---\n\n"
  - "## Prompt Example\n```text\n[Cinematography]: Medium close-up, 50mm prime lens at f/1.8, slow subtle dolly push-in, 180-degree shutter motion blur, 16:9 widescreen framing. [Subject & Action]: An artisan watchmaker in a moody wooden workshop assembling the brass gears of a mechanical balance wheel with steady five-finger precision. [Context & Negative Constraints]: Clean workbench with stationary tools, uncluttered background free of garbled text. [Style & Ambiance]: Shot on 35mm Kodak Vision3 500T film, warm directional tungsten lamplight, soft dust motes in background shadows. [Soundstage]: Rhythmic metallic ticking of clockwork, delicate click of tweezers setting a gear, quiet warm room tone.\n```\n\n---\n\n"
  - "## Verification & Error Recovery\n\n- **Verify Output**: Run `bin/agyos video self-eval <downloaded_video.mp4> --json` to check duration, resolution, fps, loudness, and black frames.\n- **Crash Recovery**: On `GENERATION_TIMEOUT`, call `flow_generate_video` or `flow_scene_extend` with `resume: true` and the saved `job_id` instead of spending credits twice.\n- **Session Timeout / Auth Refresh**: Run `bash mcp/google-flow-mcp.sh` and verify `flow_status` reports `logged_in: true`.\n"
